    {
      "id": "claim_dbb91c62335c4652817e2aa1dd856a73",
      "statement": "Promotion is a single all-or-nothing copy of candidates/<id>/manifest.json to releases/<id>/manifest.json (blobs are already in place); the copy is not isolated against concurrent promotions — the newer-release guard is check-then-act — so promote runs must be serialized (CI uses a resource group), with exit-0 guards for already-promoted ids and CI ids superseded by a higher run number (promoting an older candidate after a newer one shipped would roll production back since latest is decided by manifest upload time), and a missing candidate manifest is a hard error.",
